    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0449" n="433" xml:id="pg433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/5–1151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Deputy Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gross</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret   priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-05-11T12:52:00-04:00">May 11, 1951—12:52
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1524. Re Korea (confirming Hickerson—Gross telecon May 11 a. m.) Padilla Nervo in
                    strict confidence gave me following info Thursday, May 10, night. GOC members
                    had lengthy mtg with Rau afternoon and evening of May 10. Rau made suggestion
                    which he described as personal views not presented to or cleared by GOI. Rau
                    proposed that after adoption by GA of selective embargo res,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d285-f1"/> a second res might be adopted in following sense. GA
                    would declare as matter of policy that UN forces would not cross 38th parallel
                    on condition that (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) NK and Chi Communist forces
                    would make similar declaration, and (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) that
                    agreement would be reached on conditions “acceptable to the UC” to assure
                    security of UN forces and to assure against build-up of Chinese-NK forces.</p>
                <p>Entezam and Grafstrom apparently agreed in principle to Ran’s suggestion subject,
                    however, to Rau obtaining approval of US Govt. Padilla informed me he withheld
                    comment to Rau but was personally very favorable to the idea. Rau told GOC
                    members he would call me this a. m. to discuss matter.</p>
                <p>All three GOC members anticipate that question of further “peace moves” will
                    inevitably arise in debate on our embargo res.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gross</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
